comment on the previous scene?
Then look at the contrast of proportion and pacing. Does the next scene or section have the right
importance and length compared to the previous scene or section?
A good rule of thumb is this: find the line and keep the line. There are some scenes—such as
subplot scenes—that only set up the ť drive. Go ahead and put them in. But you can never get
away from the ť line tor too long without your story Ÿ.
